heseus/atlas/sdkjs-common.md` and its row in `INDEX.md`, and committed both as `b398de4`. The acceptance command `test -s .theseus/atlas/sdkjs-common.md` passes, and `theseus validate` reports 0 errors (1 warning about pilot mode, which was already there).\n\n**Decisions:**\n- **Index card, not a module card.** `common` is about 395k lines of `.js`, far over the 20,000-line limit. That count comes from my own `wc` over three directory levels, not from a tool, and the card says so. Following the `sdkjs-word` precedent (spec §3), the card proposes 10 submodules: api, coauth, fonts, drawings, charts, smartart, serialize, text-io, extensions and platform. It also describes the open and co-editing paths and lists the largest files.\n- **Header data left empty.** Size, languages, dependencies and metrics are `null` because there is still no `graph.json`.\n- **No follow-up packets yet.** Packets to split the module should wait until `graph.json` exists or the reviewer agrees with the split. The executor log says this.\n\n**Surprises:**\n- `docscoapi.js` contains two co-editing client classes, `CDocsCoApi` and `DocsCoApi`. Why there are two is listed as an open question.\n- `external/sdkjs/tests/` (`common/`, `runAll.js`) could serve as a test oracle, but I didn't run it, so whether it runs headless is unknown.\n- `find | xargs` and nested shell commands were refused by permissions, so I didn't work around them and took sizes from shell globs instead. My first try at appending the friction line was also refused (a `cd` combined with a redirect); it went through when run from the worktree root.\n\n**Budget:** 4 files changed against `max_files_changed: 3`. The extra files are the packet's own executor log and `friction.jsonl`, which this run requires me to update.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:** the planner should check module size before issuing a single-card packet, since both `sdkjs-word` and `sdkjs-common` ended up as index cards. Having a `graph.json` would remove most of the open questions.","ttft_ms":2104,"type":"result","duration_ms":70510,"uuid":"54dc7122-eff5-4f96-ad51-c288dec520e8","ttft_stream_ms":938,"time_to_request_ms":411,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":225,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":13,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":12,"init_frame_send":9,"engine_pickup":13,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":22,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":14,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":29,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":4,"request_build":15},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":96,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":269,"time_to_request_major_faults":3,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":239,"process_anon_mib_result":147,"process_peak_rss_mib":253,"process_cpu_ms_turn":2614,"process_wall_ms_turn":70509,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1531,"process_wall_ms_streaming":62161,"main_stream_count":12,"main_stream_event_count":1268,"main_stream_chunk_count":965,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":9,"cpu_ms":22,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":7,"ambient_wait_ms":8,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":938,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":8869938,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793644326341.2705,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"process_start_tuning":0}
